{
  "answer": "Rhysida actors use valid accounts (T1078) for access by authenticating to internal VPN access points with compromised valid credentials. [E1, E2, E3]\nAccount Use Policies (M1036) mitigate Valid Accounts (T1078) by blocking logins from non-compliant devices or outside defined organization IP ranges. [E4, E5]\nApplication Developer Guidance (M1013) mitigates Valid Accounts (T1078) by ensuring applications do not store sensitive data or credentials insecurely. [E6, E7]\nActive Directory Configuration (M1015) mitigates Valid Accounts (T1078) by disabling legacy authentication and requiring modern authentication protocols. [E8, E9]\nPassword Policies (M1027) mitigate Valid Accounts (T1078) by changing default usernames and passwords, and updating SSH keys periodically. [E10, E11]\nUser Training (M1017) mitigates Valid Accounts (T1078) by training users to only accept valid push notifications and report suspicious ones. [E12, E13]",
